   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># of VSLA groups organized</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="CARE-929" indicator-uri="https://promeva.carenederland.org/indicators.jsp/indicators.jsp?id=1" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-11-11"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-02-28"></period-end>
     <target value="120"></target>
     <actual value="36">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the first year of the project, we successfully established 36 Village Savings and Loan Association (VSLA) groups out of a planned 120, representing 30% of the overall target. While we celebrate the formation of these groups and the positive impact they will have on participating members, the project faces a challenge in meeting the initial target for Year 1. This shortfall, though significant, has provided early insights into potential barriers and opportunities.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN"># of service providers and market actors who received Gender, Equity, and Diversity training</narrative>
    </title>
    <reference code="CARE-928" indicator-uri="https://promeva.carenederland.org/indicators.jsp/indicators.jsp?id=1" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline value="0" year="2023"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-11-11"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-02-28"></period-end>
     <target value="120"></target>
     <actual value="80">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the first year of the project, we successfully trained 80 service providers and market actors on Gender, Equity, and Diversity (GED) principles out of a target of 120, representing 66.7% achievement. This signifies a strong initial mobilization and engagement of key stakeholders within our target sectors. We established effective training modules and delivery methods that resonated with participants, as evidenced by positive feedback received during and after the sessions.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
